course: dictionary
lesson: 6342
title: Words that paint a picture
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: Some words paint a picture of how something looks or how someone behaves. «Taffy sat mousy-quiet for ten whole minutes while her Daddy scratched on birch-bark with a shark's tooth.» The word quiet is the clue, so mousy here means very quiet and still.
explain: Mousy can describe hair. Mousy hair is a dull, light brown colour, like the fur of a mouse, not bright or shiny. Read the words around it to be sure you have the right meaning.
explain: Mousy can also describe a person who is quiet, shy and not easily noticed. Because it describes how someone is, it can sound unkind, so be careful before you use it about a real person.
explain: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence. «Taffy sat quiet and still for ten whole minutes» still makes sense, so mousy-quiet means very quiet and still.
fact: Mousy means like a mouse.
fact: «Mousy» hair is a dull, light brown colour.
fact: «Mousy» can describe a person who is quiet, shy and not easily noticed.
fact: «Mousy» can also mean smelling of mice, or having mice in a place.
fact: Calling a real person mousy can sound unkind, so think about how they will feel before you use it.
exercise: «Taffy sat mousy-quiet for ten whole minutes.» What does mousy-quiet suggest? | *Very quiet and still | Angry and rude | Very loud and cheerful | Wet and muddy
exercise: Mia has mousy hair. What colour is her hair? | Jet black | Bright red | *A dull, light brown | Shiny gold
exercise: Sam says the old barn smells mousy. What might this mean? | The barn has just been painted | *Mice may live there | Fresh bread is baking there | Someone has lit a bonfire
test: Which word means quiet, shy and not easily noticed? | Famished | *Mousy | Treacherous
test: Why should you be careful calling a real person mousy? | It means they are very tall | It always means they are rich | It is only a word for animals | *It can sound unkind about how they look or behave
exam: Read this: «The mousy girl sat at the back and said nothing all lesson.» What does mousy most likely mean here? | Hungry and tired | *Quiet, shy and not easily noticed | Tall and bright | Loud and funny
